  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches several call sites across error handling, UI warnings, and wallet logging to replace multiline format strings with line-by-line callback logging.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The core approach remains unchanged, with minor refinements to test coverage for platform-specific wallet naming on Windows and batch RPC whitelist requests.",
  "card": "This pull request prevents user inputs from forging log lines in debug.log by escaping embedded newlines as hex sequences in the logging subsystem. Currently, inputs like rejected RPC method names or wallet names preserve newlines, allowing restricted RPC users to inject fake log entries that can mislead node operators or log parsers. The author provides a reproducer demonstrating how an unauthorized RPC call can forge an ERROR: ConnectTip block connection failure. To keep legitimate multiline output readable, the PR introduces a line-splitting utility and updates exception, UI, and wallet logging call sites to emit each line separately.",
